## Architecture Overview

### Project Layout

```
img-settings/
├── CMakeLists.txt        # App, ImgEngine library, optional libjxl, tests
├── src/
│   ├── exif.h/.cpp       # PhotoSettings + readExif (pure, no I/O)
│   ├── jxl.h/.cpp        # JPEG XL decoding via libjxl (HAVE_JXL only)
│   ├── watermark.h/.cpp  # Engine: collect, decode, orient, resize, watermark, processFile
│   ├── processor.h/.cpp  # QML-facing Processor: thread pool, progress, cancel
│   └── main.cpp          # App entry: fonts, style selection, QML engine
├── qml/                  # UI — Main.qml (shared logic) + MacShell / WindowsShell
├── shaders/glass.frag    # Liquid Glass refraction shader
├── assets/               # App icons, Go Regular font (+ license)
├── tests/                # Qt Test unit tests + fixtures (tests/data)
├── docs/                 # User guides (EN + ES) and screenshots
├── .github/workflows/    # build.yml, ci.yml, release.yml
├── Makefile              # Developer shortcuts around CMake
└── .releaserc.json       # Semantic-release configuration
```

### Dependency Flow

```
qml/*.qml ──► Processor (src/processor.*) ──► ImgEngine (exif, watermark, jxl)
                                                   │
tests/tst_engine.cpp ──────────────────────────────┘
```

**Rule**: `ImgEngine` (`exif`, `watermark`, `jxl`) depends only on Qt GUI and libjxl. It must never include QML, Qt Quick or `processor.h`, so it stays testable without a UI. The UI talks to the engine only through `Processor`.

