## Coding Standards

### C++

| Entity | Convention | Example |
|--------|-----------|---------|
| Types | PascalCase | `PhotoSettings`, `Processor` |
| Functions, variables | camelCase | `processFile`, `outDir` |
| Members | `m_` prefix | `m_pool`, `m_generation` |
| Constants | PascalCase | `MaxWhatsAppDim`, `JpegQuality` |
| Engine API | free functions in `namespace Watermark` | `Watermark::addWatermark` |

- Use Qt types at API boundaries (`QString`, `QByteArray`, `QImage`) and `using namespace Qt::StringLiterals` (`u"..."_s`) for string literals.
- Keep helpers that are not part of the API in an anonymous namespace inside the `.cpp`.
- No raw `new`/`delete` for ownership; use parent ownership for `QObject`s and value types or smart pointers elsewhere.
- Platform differences go behind `Q_OS_MACOS` / `Q_OS_WIN` in C++ or the `fluent` flag in QML, never in the engine.

### QML

- `Main.qml` holds state and logic shared by both platforms; `MacShell.qml` and `WindowsShell.qml` only lay out the platform-specific UI.
- Design tokens live in the singletons `Theme.qml` (macOS) and `Fluent.qml` (Windows); do not hard-code colours or sizes in components.
- Use `required property` for delegate data and avoid binding loops (check the console when running).
- Glass panels must be siblings of the `Backdrop` item, because they sample the backdrop in its coordinate system.

### Error Handling

- The engine never throws. `processFile` returns an empty `QString` on success or a short, user-readable error (`"open: …"`, `"decode: …"`, `"JPEG XL: …"`).
- `readExif` never fails: missing data gives empty fields and orientation 1.
- UI errors are shown inline in the result tile or via the toast / InfoBar (`problem` signal), never by quitting.

### Concurrency

- `Processor` runs one `processFile` call per photo on a `QThreadPool` sized to `QThread::idealThreadCount()`.
- Engine functions must stay thread-safe: no shared mutable state except the font family set once at startup.
- Results return to the UI thread through queued signals. A generation counter discards results from cancelled batches.

### Comments and Documentation

- Every public function in an engine header has a one-line comment describing its contract.
- Comments explain **why**, not **what**.

