## Testing Standards

- Engine behaviour is covered by Qt Test in `tests/tst_engine.cpp` and run with CTest (`make test`).
- Prefer data-driven tests (`<test>_data()` + `QFETCH`), the Qt equivalent of table-driven tests.
- Build test inputs in code (`solidImage`, `encodeJpeg`, `withExif`) and use `QTemporaryDir` for anything that touches the filesystem. Binary fixtures go in `tests/data/` only when they cannot be generated (e.g. the JPEG XL sample) and must stay small.
- JPEG XL tests are compiled only with `HAVE_JXL`.
- Every bug fix in the engine comes with a test that fails without the fix (TDD).
- The UI is checked by the CI launch smoke test (`img-settings --smoke-test`) and by manual review of both styles. Use `IMG_SETTINGS_STYLE=windows` to preview the Windows style on macOS.

