## Development Workflow

### Git Workflow

1. `main` is the single long-lived branch. All releases are cut from `main`.
2. Work happens on short-lived branches merged through pull requests.
3. Every PR must pass CI (macOS + Windows build, unit tests and smoke test) before merge.

### Branch Naming

| Type | Pattern | Example |
|------|---------|---------|
| Feature | `feature/<short-description>` | `feature/heic-input` |
| Bug fix | `fix/<short-description>` | `fix/arw-orientation` |
| Chore / docs | `chore/<short-description>` | `chore/update-qt` |

### Commit Messages

Follow **Conventional Commits** (required by semantic-release):

```
<type>(<scope>): <subject>
```

| Type | When to use |
|------|------------|
| `feat` | New user-visible feature |
| `fix` | Bug fix |
| `docs` | Documentation only |
| `chore` | Build, CI, or tooling change |
| `refactor` | Code restructure with no behaviour change |
| `test` | Adding or fixing tests |
| `perf` | Performance improvement |

Scopes: `engine`, `ui`, `mac`, `windows`, `ci`, `build`, `deps`, `docs`.

Examples:
```
feat(engine): read EXIF from HEIC files
fix(ui): keep the window draggable from the title bar area
chore(ci): bump Qt to 6.11.3
test(engine): cover orientation values 5 and 7
```

**Breaking changes** must include `BREAKING CHANGE:` in the footer (major version bump).

### Pull Requests

- Keep PRs small and focused, describing **what** changed and **why**.
- Run `make test` locally before pushing.
- Include screenshots for UI changes (macOS and the Windows style).

