## Performance Best Practices

- Resize before watermarking so drawing happens at the final resolution.
- Decode ARW through the embedded JPEG preview first; it avoids launching external tools.
- Keep the UI thread free: all decoding and encoding happens in the thread pool. Thumbnails load asynchronously.

---

## Security Best Practices

- External tools (`dcraw`, ImageMagick) are started with `QProcess` and explicit argument lists — never through a shell.
- Only files accepted by `Watermark::isSupported` are processed; originals are never modified.
- img-settings is fully offline. Do not add network access.
- Fonts, icons and shaders are compiled into the binary as Qt resources.
